---
/**
 * /visual-financial-insights
 *
 * Angle: Data-visual learners. Show the "what."
 * Audience: People who want to see their finances, not just read numbers.
 * Intent: "I want beautiful charts and visualizations of my spending."
 * Keyword cluster: visual financial insights, spending visualization, sankey finance, money flow chart
 *
 * Narrative: Data becomes insight when it is beautifully presented.
 * Your daily entries transform into a rich visual story.
 */

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';
import AngleHero from '@/components/AngleHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import FeatureList from '@/components/FeatureList.astro';
import TrustBadge from '@/components/TrustBadge.astro';
import CTABlock from '@/components/CTABlock.astro';
import SiblingLinks from '@/components/SiblingLinks.astro';

const meta = pages.visualFinancialInsights;
---

<Layout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={`/${meta.slug}`}
>

  <AngleHero
    title="See Where Your Money Actually Goes"
    subtitle="Sankey spending flows. Portfolio breakdowns. Trend charts. Your daily entries become powerful visual insights."
    keyword="visual financial insights"
  />

  <!-- Core argument: Visualization = understanding -->
  <Section
    heading="Numbers without context are just noise."
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER:
      - Raw numbers in a spreadsheet don't tell a story
      - Visualization transforms data into understanding
      - Finzen's visuals are designed to reveal patterns, not just display data
      - The Sankey diagram as the hero feature — show how money flows
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        A list of transactions tells you what happened. A visualization tells you why it matters. Finzen is built around this distinction. Every chart, every diagram, every breakdown is designed to surface insight — not just display data.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        The centerpiece is the Sankey spending flow: a visual map of how your money moves from income to categories to savings. At a glance, you can see where the largest flows are, where you have room, and where your money is actually going.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        This is financial storytelling. And it all starts from your daily entries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- What visualizations are available -->
  <Section heading="The visual toolkit">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <FeatureList
        columns={2}
        features={[
          { label: 'Sankey Spending Flow', detail: 'See money flow from income → categories → savings in one connected diagram.' },
          { label: 'Budget vs. Actual', detail: 'Envelope budgeting with visual progress bars for each category.' },
          { label: 'Portfolio Breakdown', detail: 'Pie and bar charts showing allocation across stocks, crypto, commodities, and more.' },
          { label: 'Spending Trends', detail: 'Monthly trend lines. Spot patterns. Track improvement over time.' },
          { label: 'Net Worth Timeline', detail: 'A chart showing your financial trajectory. The long view that motivates.' },
          { label: 'Custom Date Ranges', detail: '1 month. 3 months. 1 year. Or any custom range you define.' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- How visuals emerge from daily input -->
  <Section
    heading="From 3 minutes to full insight"
    subheading="The magic is in the consistency."
    bg="stone"
  >
    {/*
      COPY PLACEHOLDER:
      - Day 1: Enter a few transactions. See a small bar chart.
      - Week 2: Patterns start to emerge. Budget tracking becomes meaningful.
      - Month 1: The Sankey flow tells a real story. Portfolio view takes shape.
      - Month 3+: Trend analysis reveals your financial trajectory.
      - The visual power comes from the daily habit, not from complexity.
    */}
    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        The visualizations in Finzen are not decorative. They are the reward for your daily habit. Every transaction you enter feeds into richer charts, clearer patterns, and deeper understanding.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        After a week, you start seeing where your money goes. After a month, budgets become meaningful. After a quarter, the trend lines tell a story about your financial health that no single number ever could.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">
        Visual insight is not instant — it compounds. That is what makes it powerful.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <TrustBadge variant="compact" />

  <CTABlock
    heading="Start building your financial story"
    subtext="Daily entries. Beautiful visualizations. A complete financial picture — over time."
  />

  <SiblingLinks slugs={['dailyExpenseTracker', 'simpleMoneyTracking']} />

</Layout>
